.TH ELECTRICITY-RUN 1 "2026-11-13" "electricity 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
electricity-run \- run a Circuitry orchestration the way cof run does (preview)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
electricity run <orchestration.yml> [-e key=value]... [--config config.json]
[--out state.json] [--live-state state.json] [--events events.jsonl]
[--allow-capabilities cap,cap] [--adapter name] [--label TEXT] [--quiet]
[--pretty] [--profile <path>] [--state state.json] [--resume MODE] [--force]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
electricity is a preview: it runs
tool/dynamic/if/finally/loop/use/yield/prompt/reflector documents only
(persistence and runtime plugins are refused with a preview marker; use \fBcof
run\fR for those). A prompt effect's model is reached for real through a
document's \fBadapter:\fR or a prompt's \fBprovider:\fR, including
\fBollama\fR, the OpenAI-compatible family, \fBopenai\fR, \fBanthropic\fR,
\fBreplicate\fR, \fBwatsonx\fR, \fBcyberdiner\fR, \fBclaude_code\fR, \fBpi\fR,
and the \fBscripted\fR adapter; \fBlitellm\fR has no electricity builder and
is refused permanently.
.PP
\fBelectricity run <doc>\fR accepts the same options \fBcof run\fR does, with
the same config discovery (\fB--config\fR optional: CIRCUITRY_CONFIG, then a
trusted project config in the working directory, then the global config) and
the same meaning for --allow-capabilities/--adapter/--quiet. The legacy
\fBelectricity <config.json> <doc>\fR form (config always explicit, never
discovered) keeps working as an alias; --profile/--pretty/--dump-ir are
electricity-only additions, available under either form.
.PP
\fBelectricity man [run]\fR shows the electricity(1) or electricity-run(1) man
page through \fBman\fR on a terminal, or prints its roff when piped or given
--roff.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --help
Print this message and exit.
.TP
.B -e
\fIkey=value\fR Pass an orchestration input, checked against its declared
interface.inputs. Repeatable; a later -e for the same key wins.
.TP
.B --config, -c
\fIpath\fR Path to config JSON, or CIRCUITRY_CONFIG, or the same discovery cof
run uses. The legacy form's first positional is this value, always explicit;
--config/-c is rejected there as redundant.
.TP
.B --out, -o
\fIpath\fR Write the final state to <path> instead of stdout. The -o alias is
run only.
.TP
.B --pretty
Sort state keys and indent by 2 spaces in the final state, whether printed to
stdout or written to --out.
.TP
.B --live-state
\fIpath\fR Mirror the running state to <path> as it changes.
.TP
.B --events
\fIpath\fR Write a JSONL event stream to <path>.
.TP
.B --allow-capabilities
\fIcap,cap\fR Comma-separated capabilities to pre-approve for this run.
.TP
.B --adapter
\fIname\fR This run's default adapter, beating a loaded --profile, the
orchestration and the config.
.TP
.B --label
\fItext\fR Literal text for this run's label, beating the document's top-level
label: template. Never rendered. Cleaned the same way either way: whitespace
collapsed to one space, control characters and escape sequences dropped,
trimmed, cut at 64 characters; empty after cleaning means no label.
.TP
.B --quiet
Suppress non-essential output (accepted for parity).
.TP
.B --profile
\fIpath\fR Load a profile (adapter/model/inputs/persistence overrides, routing
pins and provider denials) from an explicit path -- no name discovery.
.TP
.B --state, -s
\fIpath\fR Resume from this saved state file -- every top-level key it
carries, not just input. A named effect whose saved node already finished
without error is skipped and reused only when --resume is also given.
.TP
.B --resume
\fImode\fR Combined with --state <file>: skip a named effect whose saved node
already finished without error. cof run's 'last'/a run-id mode is not
supported -- --resume always needs --state <file> naming the saved state
directly. Refuses a document that changed since the saved run unless --force.
.TP
.B --force
With --resume, continue even though the orchestration's content changed since
the saved run (or it carries no recorded digest at all).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B electricity config.json orchestration.yml -e name=world --pretty
Runs a document directly, with one input, and a sorted/indented final state on
stdout.
.TP
.B electricity run orchestration.yml --out state.json
Runs a document through the same config discovery and options cof run uses,
writing the final state to a file instead of stdout.
.TP
.B electricity run orchestration.yml --state state.json --resume continue
Resumes a previous run from its saved state, skipping any named effect that
already finished without error.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CIRCUITRY_CONFIG
An explicit config JSON path, for electricity run's discovery (same as
--config; when set, replaces the global config and any project config
entirely, rather than layering on top of them). The legacy form's first
positional is always explicit and never consults this variable.
.TP
.B CIRCUITRY_MODEL
Overrides the resolved config's default_model.
.TP
.B CIRCUITRY_ADAPTER
Overrides the resolved config's default_adapter.
.TP
.B CIRCUITRY_ADAPTER_URL
Overrides the resolved default adapter's base_url.
.TP
.B CIRCUITRY_COMFYUI_URL
Overrides the comfyui plugin's base_url.
.TP
.B CIRCUITRY_SYSTEMONE_URL
Overrides the systemone plugin's base_url.
.TP
.B CIRCUITRY_ENABLED_ADAPTERS
Comma-separated allowlist, narrowing (never widening) the resolved config's
enabled_adapters.
.TP
.B CIRCUITRY_ENABLED_PLUGINS
Comma-separated allowlist, narrowing (never widening) the resolved config's
enabled_plugins.
.TP
.B CIRCUITRY_ENABLED_TOOLS
Comma-separated allowlist, narrowing (never widening) the resolved config's
enabled_tools.
.TP
.B CIRCUITRY_ENVIRONMENT
Overrides the resolved config's environment (dev, prod, or test).
.TP
.B CIRCUITRY_TRUST_PROJECT_CONFIG
Trusts a project config in the current directory without running cof trust
first.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/circuitry/config.json
The global config, applied first; a trusted project config layers on top of
it.
.TP
.I ~/.config/circuitry/.env
Private environment variables, loaded before config resolution (the same file
cof setup writes).
.TP
.I ~/.config/circuitry/trusted.json
Project configs trusted by cof trust; electricity run's discovery consults it
the same way cof run does.
.TP
.I ./circuitry.config.json, ./config.json
A project config in the working directory, layered on top of the global config
once trusted.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
The run failed, the orchestration was not found, or the config could not be
read.
.TP
.B 2
A usage error -- an unrecognized option, a missing required argument, or an
unknown electricity man page.
.TP
.B 129
The run was interrupted by SIGHUP.
.TP
.B 130
The run was interrupted by SIGINT (Ctrl-C).
.TP
.B 143
The run was interrupted by SIGTERM.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR electricity (1),
.BR electricity\-run (1),
.BR cof (1),
.BR cof\-run (1),
.BR osi (1)
